      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Of course, here's a version that incorporates more details without being redundant:\n\n\"In preparing the dish, quarter the chicken breast for manageable pieces. Warm olive oil in a large pan over medium heat. Season both sides of the chicken with a modest amount of salt and freshly cracked pepper. Introduce thinly sliced garlic to the pan, allowing the pungent flavor to infuse into the oil without burning. Simmer chicken until it's crisped to a golden-brown. Now, decant a cup of velvety heavy cream into the pan, bringing it to a gentle simmer as the chicken cooks. Stir in a generous helping of finely grated Parmesan cheese until the sauce begins to thicken. Once the sauce is velvishly smooth, ladle it onto a warm bed of al dente pasta, ensuring each bite is wrapped in the creamy, garlic-infused oil and cheese concoction.\"",
